    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d407">

                <pb facs="0464" n="292" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4918</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Nicaraguan Chargé</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Cuadra Zavala</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 36</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 2, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of May 19,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d407-f1"/> in which you
                    state that you are instructed by the President of Nicaragua to inform me that
                    the Nicaraguan Congress has passed a resolution severing the relations of the
                    Nicaraguan Government with the Imperial German Government, and has authorized
                    him to offer to the Government of the United States the use of the ports and
                    territorial waters of Nicaragua during the present war.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to say that it affords me pleasure to accept, on behalf
                    of this Government, your Government’s highly <pb facs="0465" n="293"
                        xml:id="pg293"/> valued offer. I beg to request that you will convey to
                    President Chamorro this Government’s thanks for, and high appreciation of the
                    aid thus extended by his administration, and my heartfelt gratification at the
                    new bonds of amity thus added to the ties of friendship that so happily exist
                    between the two Governments.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
